18:38:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-07T12:34:48Z","closed_at":"2025-04-07T13:46:47Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101003","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101003","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101003.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101003.patch","merged_at":"2025-04-07T13:46:47Z"},"body":"A big reason the above issue happened in the first place is because SO MUCH of the enum binding logic happens after the fact, when the overwhelming majority could be determined via `<type_traits>` magic. The only exception seems to be the qualified name, which this PR keeps as an explicitly provided variable; absolutely *everything* else is now handled natively. While this could probably be implemented more cleanly via C++20 concepts, the **entire bindsystem** would benefit from them; so for now, SFINAE[^1] gets the job done.\r\n\r\nEDIT: No longer a fix for #101002, as the option I tried exploring here increased binary size to a non-insignificant degree\r\n\r\n[^1]: https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/sfinae","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_ur